                    briefing_text_r2:       `Convert the prioritized gaps into a program blueprint within the <strong>€900,000</strong> fixed budget. Full-fidelity design for all six gaps and 300 people costs ~€1.05M — over the cap and into negative margin — so you must <strong>prioritize, not wish-list</strong>. Map methods to behaviour: feedback and role-authority skills are <em>built</em> through practice, observation and coaching, not <em>lectured about</em>. Choose your scope, your dominant method, the depth of coaching and application projects, and whether each module ships with a behaviour-change measurement plan. Backward design means every element earns its place against the metric the client will judge.`,
