                    coach_r4_mandate:       `<strong>Mandating attendance buys bodies in seats, not belief.</strong> The resistant manager who thinks “culture isn’t my job” needs to see it as <em>his</em> retention and team-performance problem — not just another required course.`,
                    coach_r4_drop:          `<strong>Optional culture modules gut the diagnosis.</strong> The managers who most need the feedback and role-authority work are exactly the ones who will opt out. The culture work is the programme, not an extra.`,
                    coach_r4_outcome:       `<strong>That is an evidence plan a CHRO will accept.</strong> Behaviour metrics, retention and promotion-readiness are the outcomes the €900k was justified against — and the proof that protects the month-six NPS and renews the account.`,
                    coach_r4_smile:         `<strong>A smile-sheet won’t renew a €2.5M account.</strong> A satisfaction score satisfies on day one and proves nothing about whether the diagnosis was right. The CHRO is asking about retention and promotion-readiness — measure those.`,

                    sum_default:            `Decision made.`,
