                    sum_r2_error:           `Wish-list scope or lectured a built competency.`,
                    sum_r2_weak:            `Blueprint under-built for behaviour change.`,
                    sum_r3_good:            `Led with the outcome, priced right, won both stakeholders.`,
                    sum_r3_weak:            `Buried the reframe, mispriced, or lost a stakeholder.`,
                    sum_r4_good:            `Defended the diagnosis with an outcome evidence plan.`,
                    sum_r4_weak:            `Capitulated or measured only satisfaction.`,

                    insight_reframe:        `You won on the real problem: a reframed diagnosis, led with the client’s outcome, priced inside the cap, and defended with outcome evidence. Needs-fit is high and the account is durable — exactly the growth engine LLP is built on.`,
                    insight_literal:        `You won the deal and failed the client. The literal-build proposal satisfies on day one and disappoints at month six — the managers can run a calendar and still won’t give feedback, and retention hasn’t moved. The account erodes instead of growing to €2.5M.`,
                    insight_lost:           `The two literal-build rivals out-positioned you and won the RFP. A correct diagnosis the client never registered — or one that read as ignoring their brief — does not win. Reframing is a positioning act, not just an analytical one.`,
                    insight_compromised:    `You stayed in the running but the diagnosis was diluted. Win probability held, yet needs-fit is too thin to protect the month-six NPS or grow the account. Lead harder with the outcome and protect the design.`,
                    insight_overbudget:     `You breached the €900,000 fixed cap. A blueprint that costs more than the budget is not a bid — a fixed budget forces a priority, not a wish-list.`,
                    insight_margin:         `You priced below the 20% margin floor. Winning on a price you lose money at damages the unit, not just this deal.`,
                    insight_account:        `Account health is low — month-six NPS and the €2.5M pipeline are at risk. The cost of mis-scoping is paid when the programme fails to move the metric the client later cares about.`,
                    insight_growth:         `This is the durable account: a programme that solved the real problem, evidence the client accepts, and an NPS that turns a €900k deal into a €2.5M+/year relationship.`,

                    hint_overbudget:        `Your design cost is over the €900k fixed cap. Re-scope: prioritize the two highest-impact gaps and sequence the rest to phase two.`,
                    hint_margin:            `Your price is below the €720k margin floor. Winning on a loss-making price damages the unit — protect the 20% margin.`,
                    hint_fit:               `Needs-fit is weak. You are drifting toward the literal brief; reframe the root gaps and map practice-led methods to the competencies that must change.`,
                    hint_win:               `Win probability is low. Lead page one with the client’s business outcome and evidence why the literal ask fails — positioning is what raises the win odds of the correct diagnosis.`,
                    hint_account:           `Account health is sliding. Defend the diagnosis without capitulating, and commit a month-six evidence plan on behaviour, retention and promotion-readiness.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — needs-fit, win probability and account health all healthy. Lock in the outcome evidence plan so the account grows past month six.`,

